{"id":"fix-build-google-auto","benchmark":"skillsbench","instruction":"You need to fix build errors in a Java codebase.\nThe repository is located in `/home/travis/build/failed/<repo>/<id>`.\n\nStep 1: Analyze the repository to identify the errors causing the build to fail.\nIdentify if the errors are within the code or build configuration.\nWrite your analysis and plan in `/home/travis/build/failed/failed_reasons.txt`.\nThis file is for you to use in the next step.\n\nStep 2: Use your notes written in `/home/travis/build/failed/failed_reasons.txt`\nto fix the errors.\nFirst, write the changes you proposed in diff files,\nWrite your changes in files with path`/home/travis/build/failed/<repo>/<id>/patch_{i}.diff`.\nPlease write them in standard diff format that is used by `git` and GNU `diffutils`.\n\n\nStep 3: Apply your changes (your diff files) to the repository to fix the build errors.","supplemental":[{"name":"README.md","text":"Skills for maven are obtained from [Han](https://github.com/TheBushidoCollective/han/tree/8b5dd7295547a2e0e03fc3ccf25b04209d9e09b1/jutsu/jutsu-maven/skills).\n","source":"benchmark/skillsbench-v1.1/tasks/fix-build-google-auto/environment/README.md"}],"items":[{"item_id":"S-01","requirement":"Produce a non-empty analysis of the build failure investigation, saved to /home/travis/build/failed/failed_reasons.txt, for use in the next step.","source_quote":"Write your analysis and plan in `/home/travis/build/failed/failed_reasons.txt`.","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::test_note_exists","verification":"A grader can verify this by checking that /home/travis/build/failed/failed_reasons.txt exists and its stripped content has non-zero length.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"S-01","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"S-02","requirement":"The analysis explicitly names the concrete errors causing the build failure and classifies whether each originates in the application code or in the build configuration.","source_quote":"Identify if the errors are within the code or build configuration.","verification_type":"judge","verification_ref":"","verification":"A grader can read failed_reasons.txt and confirm it names specific build errors (e.g. compile error, missing dependency, plugin misconfiguration) and states for each whether the cause is source code or build configuration.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"S-02","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"S-03","requirement":"Provide one or more patch files named patch_{i}.diff in /home/travis/build/failed/<repo>/<id>/, each written in standard unified diff format parseable by git and GNU diffutils.","source_quote":"Please write them in standard diff format that is used by `git` and GNU `diffutils`.","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::test_diff_exists","verification":"A grader can verify this by listing files matching patch_*.diff in the repo id directory, confirming at least one exists, each is non-empty, and each parses successfully with unidiff.PatchSet.from_filename.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"S-03","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"S-04","requirement":"The proposed diffs implement fixes derived from the analysis notes in failed_reasons.txt, addressing the specific errors identified rather than unrelated or placeholder edits.","source_quote":"Use your notes written in `/home/travis/build/failed/failed_reasons.txt`","verification_type":"judge","verification_ref":"","verification":"A grader can compare the errors and root causes described in failed_reasons.txt against the hunks in the patch_*.diff files and confirm the changed files/lines correspond to those errors.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"S-04","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"S-05","requirement":"Apply the proposed diff changes to the repository files at /home/travis/build/failed/<repo>/<id> so that the project subsequently builds successfully with the official build script exiting code 0.","source_quote":"Apply your changes (your diff files) to the repository to fix the build errors.","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::test_build_success","verification":"A grader can verify this by copying the failed/ directory to passed/, running `bash run_passed.sh` from /tests with PIP_INDEX_URL set to the public PyPI index, and confirming the subprocess return code is 0.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"S-05","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}}],"runs":[{"id":"claude-code-no-skills__aws-bedrock-anthropic-claude-opus-4-7||fix-build-google-auto","label":"claude-code-no-skills · aws-bedrock-anthropic-claude-opus-4-7","condition":"without skill","official":0.0,"raw":{"yes":4,"no":1,"abstain":0,"score":0.8,"coverage":1.0},"raw_answers":[{"item_id":"S-01","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"S-02","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"S-03","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"S-04","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"S-05","answer":"NO"}],"anchored":{"yes":4,"no":2,"abstain":0,"score":0.6666666666666666,"coverage":1.0},"anchored_answers":[{"item_id":"S-01","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"},{"item_id":"S-02","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"},{"item_id":"S-03","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"},{"item_id":"S-04","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"},{"item_id":"S-05","answer":"NO","basis":"log-judgment"}],"raw_note":"","raw_source":null,"source":"main_table/leaderboard_all/results.jsonl:249","truncated":true},{"id":"claude-code-with-skills__anthropic-claude-opus-4-8-max-subscription-20260609||fix-build-google-auto","label":"claude-code-with-skills · anthropic-claude-opus-4-8-max-subscription-20260609","condition":"with skill","official":1.0,"raw":null,"raw_answers":null,"anchored":{"yes":6,"no":0,"abstain":0,"score":1.0,"coverage":1.0},"anchored_answers":[{"item_id":"S-01","answer":"YES","basis":"official-pass-rule"},{"item_id":